> Use reset_index() (without drop=True) if:
You want to keep the original index as a column for reference. It is used to remove the multi-index (if any) and create a simple, sequential integer index. It helps simplify the structure of the DataFrame for easier processing.
> Use reset_index(drop=True) if:
You want to completely discard the original index and start with a clean integer index. It ensures that the old index is not added as a column in the final DataFrame, which would be unnecessary and potentially confusing for further operations.

Ex:
